        "Node name for S&R": "MiniMaxH3ImageToVideo"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Use the uploaded Axon Signal frame as the absolute visual anchor. Preserve the\nsame original engineer, face, graphite utility suit, amber shoulder line,\nsignal prism, observatory architecture, palette, lens, and lighting.\n\nCreate a 10-second, 16:9 cinematic continuation.\n\n[0–3s] Begin from the exact reference composition. The engineer raises the\nblack prism by a few centimeters. The amber channel brightens gradually while\nthe camera makes a restrained five-percent push-in.\n\n[3–7s] The engineer turns toward the circular antenna. Keep identity and outfit\nstable. A single amber signal travels from the prism across the concrete floor.\nUse physically plausible cloth and wind motion.\n\n[7–10s] The camera slides to a three-quarter profile as the signal reaches the\nantenna. One amber ring expands into the clouds; reflections move across the\nengineer's visor. Hold the final frame for half a second.\n\nAudio: native stereo electrical hum, wind, three relay clicks, one deep analog\npulse. No dialogue. Do not redesign the subject, add characters, change the\nlocation, invent text, distort the hands, or introduce logos and watermarks.",
        1344,
        768,
        73
      ]
